codex
The proof architecture is now shifting from a purely functional evaluator to an operational `<k>`-cell evaluator. That matters for symbolic execution: K can branch on the unknown length and endpoint equality, while a function equation only fires when its side condition is already known. The recursive-call continuation will also make the induction hypothesis match directly.
